{
  "file": "crates/trust-but-verify/tests/support/stored_graph.rs",
  "item": "impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[outgoing_edges]",
  "citations": [
    {
      "role": "cite",
      "name": "habeas:coverage",
      "commentary": "Domain requires this callback even for a storage-only consumer. The\n delegation test must use only node_path; discovering edges would be\n an unwanted graph access, which this guard rejects. Traversal fixtures\n separately exercise edge discovery."
    }
  ],
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation on `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/support/stored_graph.rs#impl[StoredGraph/Domain]/fn[outgoing_edges]` meets the built-in's criteria.\n\n- **Form:** The citation is a fenced citation commentary on an explicit function with a body. That is a permitted form, and the commentary is tracked.\n- **Substance:** The reason is substantive. `Domain` requires the callback. This storage-only fixture deliberately forbids edge discovery, so the body is a guard that panics. The guard is meant to stay unexecuted, which makes the missing coverage acceptable. The commentary does not rest on difficulty.\n- **Agreement with source:** The body of `outgoing_edges` is `panic!(\"storage operations must not discover graph edges\")`, which matches the stated guard.\n  - `load_evidence` and `store_evidence` in `impl[StoredGraph/Domain]` delegate to `FileEvidenceStorage` using only `self.node_path(node)`. They never call `outgoing_edges`.\n  - The delegation test, `tests/storage.rs#fn[consumer_delegates_evidence_storage_using_only_the_requested_nodes_path]`, uses only `load_evidence`, `store_evidence` and `node_path`.\n  - The other storage test, `fn[malformed_records_are_storage_errors_and_bad_outputs_are_output_errors]`, calls `validation::verify`, `store_evidence` and `load_evidence`. Nothing in it exercises edge discovery.\n- **Other fixtures:** The claim that traversal fixtures separately exercise edge discovery is supported. `tests/contracts.rs` has other `Domain` implementations with real `outgoing_edges` bodies, in `impl[Application/Domain]` and in the `Relationships` implementation.\n\nI found no gap.",
